# Environment variables kosong reads.
#
# None of these are required. kosong works with all of them unset.
# This file documents them; it is not loaded automatically.
#
# For the API's own secrets, see apps/api/.dev.vars.example — those are set with
# `wrangler secret put` and never live in a file in production.

# Which editor `kosong edit` opens. Standard Unix variables; VISUAL wins.
# kosong runs this directly, never through a shell, so shell syntax such as
# `;` or `|` is refused rather than silently misinterpreted.
# EDITOR="nano"
# VISUAL="code --wait"

# Disables colour. Any value, including empty, per the NO_COLOR convention.
# NO_COLOR=1

# Where kosong keeps settings. Defaults to the platform location:
#   macOS  ~/Library/Application Support/kosong
#   Linux  ~/.config/kosong
#
# Setting this also selects an isolated profile: the sign-in is kept beside the
# settings rather than in the shared system keychain, so two profiles do not
# silently share one account.
# KOSONG_CONFIG_DIR="$HOME/.config/kosong"

# Forces the sign-in credential into a specific file rather than the keychain.
# For tests and CI, which must never touch a developer's real keychain.
# KOSONG_SESSION_FILE="/tmp/kosong-test-session"

# The API to talk to. Point this at a local Worker during development.
# KOSONG_API_URL="http://127.0.0.1:8787"
